### ============================================
### JWT REST API Test Suite
### Server: https://localhost:8443
### Both /auth/* and /v1/auth/* paths are supported
### Run sequentially — each step depends on the previous
### ============================================

### ========== SETUP ==========

### 1. Healthcheck (should return 200 + database:true)
GET https://localhost:8443/v1/api/health
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. Register alice (should return 201)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 3. Register bob (should return 201)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "geheim456"
}

### ========== LOGIN + TOKEN SAVE ==========

### 4. Login as alice (save token)
# @name loginAlice
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Save Alice's token
@alice_token = {{loginAlice.response.body.token}}

### 5. Login as bob (save token)
# @name loginBob
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "geheim456"
}

### Save Bob's token
@bob_token = {{loginBob.response.body.token}}

### ========== REGISTRATION / LOGIN ERRORS ==========

### 6. Register with short password (should return 400)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "charlie",
  "password": "short"
}

### 7. Register with invalid username (should return 400)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user@name!",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 8. Register duplicate username (should return 409)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 9. Login without password (should return 400)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice"
}

### 10. Login wrong password (should return 401)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong_password"
}

### 11. Login with legacy path /auth/ instead of /v1/auth/ (should return 200)
POST https://localhost:8443/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### ========== UPDATE PASSWORD ==========

### 12. Update password (alice) — requires token (should return 200)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/password
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "newSecret456"
}

### 13. Login with OLD password (should return 401 — old password invalid)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 14. Login with NEW password (save new token) (should return 200)
# @name loginAliceNew
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "newSecret456"
}

### Save Alice's new token
@alice_token = {{loginAliceNew.response.body.token}}

### ========== UPDATE USERNAME ==========

### 15. Update username (alice -> alice_updated) — requires token (should return 200)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/username
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice_updated"
}

### 16. Login with OLD username (should return 401 — old username gone)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "newSecret456"
}

### 17. Login with NEW username (save fresh token) (should return 200)
# @name loginAliceUpdated
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice_updated",
  "password": "newSecret456"
}

### Save Alice's new token after username change
@alice_token = {{loginAliceUpdated.response.body.token}}

### ========== AUTH-REQUIRED OPERATIONS (ERRORS) ==========

### 18. Update password without token (should return 401)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "hacked1234"
}

### 19. Update username without token (should return 401)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/username
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "hacker"
}

### 20. Delete user without token (should return 401)
DELETE https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/delete
Content-Type: application/json

### 21. Update password with invalid token (should return 401)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/password
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "hacked1234"
}

### ========== DELETE ==========

### 22. Delete bob — requires token (should return 200)
DELETE https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/delete
Authorization: Bearer {{bob_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 23. Login as deleted user bob (should return 401)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "geheim456"
}

### ========== MISCELLANEOUS ERRORS ==========

### 24. Wrong HTTP method on register (should return 405)
GET https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

### 25. Non-existent path (should return 404)
GET https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/nonexistent
Content-Type: application/json

### ============================================
### Expected status codes:
### 200 OK - Success
### 201 Created - User registered
### 400 Bad Request - Missing/invalid fields
### 401 Unauthorized - Login failed / No token / Invalid token
### 404 Not Found - User not found (delete/update non-existent)
### 405 Method Not Allowed - Wrong HTTP method
### 409 Conflict - Username already exists
### 429 Too Many Requests - Rate limit exceeded
### 503 Service Unavailable - Database down
### ============================================
